course: dictionary
lesson: 665
title: One word, many meanings: bake
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word bake has more than one meaning, so the sentence tells you which one to use. Ask yourself what is being baked. «You smell cookies baking from the other room» means cooking food in an oven, because cookies are food.
explain: The second meaning is about heat making something hard. Clay and bricks can be baked until they are firm. The clue is what the thing is, not just the word bake.
explain: The third meaning is a joke about heat. «We're baking in the sun» means we are very hot, not that we are in an oven. Check by swapping in your meaning and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Bake is a verb: bake, bakes, baked, baking. It can also be a noun: a bake.
fact: To bake means to cook food in an oven with dry heat, like bread, cakes or cookies.
fact: To bake can mean to make something hard by heat, like clay or bricks.
fact: «We're baking in the sun» means we are very hot.
fact: A bake sale is run with an adult's help, with clean hands and clear prices.
exercise: «You smell cookies baking from the other room.» What does baking mean here? | Shouting loudly | Sleeping under a blanket | Running very fast | *Cooking in an oven
exercise: «We're baking in the sun.» What does baking mean here? | *Very hot | Being paid for work | Cooking dinner | Making clay hard
exercise: «A lemonade stand or bake sale is run with an adult's help.» What is a bake sale most likely? | A race around the park | *Selling baked food, with an adult's help | Teaching a dog to sit | Digging a hole in the garden
test: «The clay was baked until it was hard.» What does baked mean here? | *Made hard by heat | Cooked as a cake | Sold at a sale | Very hot in the sun
test: «Before a loaf of bread reaches you, many people work on it: a farmer grows wheat, a miller grinds flour, a baker bakes.» Who bakes the bread? | A shopkeeper | A driver | A farmer | *A baker
exam: Which form in this list is a noun? bake, bakes, baked, baking, a bake | *a bake | bake | baked | baking
